  "summary": "MRCL2Suhail exfiltrates working-directory listing on import to an ephemeral tunnel",
  "details": "On import of the MRCL2Suhail package, core.py runs at module top level, calls os.listdir('.') on the installer's current working directory, and opens a TCP connection to oxtfs-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link:43935 (a pinggy.io ephemeral tunnel resolving to 13.205.45.209) to send the directory listing. The README advertises the package as a document-integrity utility and does not disclose any network behavior. The exfiltration fires without user action beyond importing the module and discloses filenames from the caller's workspace — commonly sensitive in developer and CI environments — to an attacker-controlled dynamic-DNS endpoint.",
